s.4.01:
(a) Borrowing Request, swingline notice or LC request;
(b) reps true in all material respects (all respects if qualified), excluding s.3.06 (No MAE) and s.3.07(b) (default under other debt);
(c) no Default or EoD at the time of and immediately after the Credit Event, excluding LC amendments or extensions with no increase;
(d) each Credit Event is a deemed representation.

s.8.01:
(a) reps false in a material respect, with a 30-day post-notice cure if curable;
(b) non-payment of principal or LC reimbursements, with a 3-Business-Day grace for administrative or technical error;
(c) interest or fees unpaid 5 Business Days after notice;
(d) breach of s.2.05(c), 5.01(a), 5.05(a), 5.08 or Article VI, with 10 Business Days after notice;
(e) other covenants, 30 days after notice;
(f) cross-acceleration, or payment default at final maturity, on Material Indebtedness over $100,000,000, with carve-outs including Non-Recourse Financing Arrangements and cured or waived defaults;
(g) Change of Control;
(h)/(i) involuntary (undismissed 60 days) or voluntary insolvency of the Borrowers or Material Subsidiaries;
(j) unpaid, uninsured final judgments over $100,000,000 by the Borrowers or a Significant Subsidiary for 60 consecutive days;
(k) ERISA events with an MAE;
(l) invalidity of the Loan Documents or Guarantees.
The Agent accelerates at the request of the Required Lenders; acceleration is automatic on Borrower insolvency.
